{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Make for yourself two silver trumpets.</b> Since the intention now was to journey, to bring them into the land immediately, He commanded making trumpets for a king's fanfare with them — when the Tabernacle travels, when the sanctuary travels, and when they go out to battle, as it says: וְכִי תָבֹאוּ מִלְחָמָה בְּאַרְצְכֶם עַל הַצַּר הַצֹּרֵר אֶתְכֶם וַהֲרֵעֹתֶם בַּחֲצֹצְרֹת (Numbers 10:9)." "<b>And they shall be for you for summoning the assembly.</b> Because the summoning of the assembly and the princes was to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting before HaShem, He wanted their summons to be by trumpets, for the honor of the King."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:13.906382861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}